From 0e72cc59c956b78fe12172cec7bd14d0f09ad651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Syed Labeeq Sajid Bukhari <syedlabeeq@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:16:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] libkmod: fix type confusion in kmod_module_get_sections()
 error path

The fail: path of kmod_module_get_sections() releases the partially
built list with kmod_module_unref_list(), but the list elements are
struct kmod_module_section, not struct kmod_module.

kmod_module_unref() on a section object first reads and decrements
mod->refcount, which sits at offset 80 of struct kmod_module, while a
section allocation is only 8 + strlen(name) + 1 bytes (~17-25 bytes)
-- an out-of-bounds read+write on the heap. If the decremented value
happens to be <= 0, execution continues with mod->ctx aliasing
section->address and mod->path/mod->hashkey aliasing the section name
bytes, leading to wild dereferences and frees of semi-controlled
pointers (kmod_pool_del_module, kmod_module_unref_list(mod->dep),
free(mod->path)).

The bug is reachable through the public API kmod_module_get_sections()
(used by modinfo) whenever the loop over /sys/module/<mod>/sections/
fails mid-iteration after at least one section was appended: an
openat/read failure (e.g. module unload race or an unreadable section
file) or a malloc failure.

The function's own API documentation in libkmod.h states the returned
list must be freed with kmod_module_section_free_list(); the error
path is the only place that violates this.

Fix it by freeing the list with kmod_module_section_free_list(), as
the success path and the API contract already do.

Link: https://github.com/kmod-project/kmod/pull/467
Signed-off-by: Lucas De Marchi <demarchi@kernel.org>
---
 libkmod/libkmod-module.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libkmod/libkmod-module.c b/libkmod/libkmod-module.c
index 2248acf2..17dce973 100644
--- a/libkmod/libkmod-module.c
+++ b/libkmod/libkmod-module.c
@@ -1748,7 +1748,7 @@ KMOD_EXPORT struct kmod_list *kmod_module_get_sections(const struct kmod_module
 
 fail:
 	closedir(d);
-	kmod_module_unref_list(list);
+	kmod_module_section_free_list(list);
 	return NULL;
 }
 
